\newlabel{eq:flattening}{{8}{11}{One dial between the two regimes}{equation.6.8}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The flattening law. As the data eigenvalue $\lambda \to 1$, the optimal attention rate $\eta $ obeys $1 - \eta \propto \sqrt  {1 - \lambda }$ and the effective window $1/(1-\eta )$ diverges: sharp associative patterns flatten into counting. Closed form against numerical optimization, agreement to six decimals; window $1.4 \to 75$ across $\lambda \in [0.5, 0.9999]$.}}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flattening}{{4}{11}{The flattening law. As the data eigenvalue $\lambda \to 1$, the optimal attention rate $\eta $ obeys $1 - \eta \propto \sqrt {1 - \lambda }$ and the effective window $1/(1-\eta )$ diverges: sharp associative patterns flatten into counting. Closed form against numerical optimization, agreement to six decimals; window $1.4 \to 75$ across $\lambda \in [0.5, 0.9999]$}{figure.4}{}}
